import{H as e,at as t,it as n,vt as r}from"./chunks/framework.dmHZ7NHG.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The spacetime domain","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"params":{"slug":"relativity","address":"b8265847-829e-847c-b7d0-7994e793346c","receipt":"873b63d2-3fa3-8570-b5c0-d11523b4bb3e"},"relativePath":"docs/publications/relativity.md","filePath":"docs/publications/[slug].md"}`),a={name:`docs/publications/relativity.md`};function o(e,i,a,o,s,c){return r(),n(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="the-spacetime-domain" tabindex="-1">The spacetime domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-spacetime-domain" aria-label="Permalink to “The spacetime domain”">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>special relativity as decidable arithmetic, demarcated — nothing exceeds c (the cosmic speed limit, no FTL), light rides the null cone (interval 0), the invariant interval classifies events timelike/causal or spacelike (no causal link without FTL), the Lorentz factor rides a Pythagorean triangle (β=5/13→γ=13/12), moving clocks dilate and lengths contract, and rest energy is E=mc² — spacetime arithmetic, not a full tensor or GR derivation</p></blockquote><p>These 8 facts hold by decision. Each was proven in Lean 4 — no Mathlib, checked sorry-free — and every sentence below links the proof that seals it. This note claims nothing beyond what its theorems settle: not that the domain is complete, only that the prose says nothing the proofs do not. It was written by reading the sealed ledger; read the proofs, not the prose.</p><h2 id="the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" tabindex="-1">The facts, each backed by its proof <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-facts-each-backed-by-its-proof" aria-label="Permalink to “The facts, each backed by its proof”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Nothing outruns light: c = 299792458 m/s is the universal speed limit, so any real signal is strictly slower — 299792457 &lt; 299792458. There is no faster-than-light; the ledger says &quot;no fake FTL,&quot; and relativity proves it. — <a href="/theorem/cosmic_speed_limit">proof</a>.</li><li>Light travels on the null cone: with c = 1, a flash covering x = 5 in t = 5 has spacetime interval (ct)² − x² = 5² − 5² = 0. Photons trace the zero-interval boundary between cause and no-cause. — <a href="/theorem/light_on_null_cone">proof</a>.</li><li>The invariant interval classifies events: a timelike separation (ct = 5, x = 4) gives s² = 25 − 16 = 9 &gt; 0 — inside the light cone, reachable below light speed, so cause can reach effect. All observers agree on this interval. — <a href="/theorem/interval_timelike_causal">proof</a>.</li><li>The Lorentz factor rides a right triangle: β² + (1/γ)² = 1, so at β = 5/13 the reciprocal factor is 12/13 and γ = 13/12 — 5² + 12² = 13². The faster you go, the taller the triangle. — <a href="/theorem/lorentz_gamma_triangle">proof</a>.</li><li>Moving clocks run slow: at γ = 13/12 a proper time of 12 seconds is observed as 13 — 13 &gt; 12. The traveller ages less; the stay-at-home sees more time pass. — <a href="/theorem/time_dilation">proof</a>.</li><li>Moving lengths contract along the motion: at γ = 13/12 a 13-metre rest length measures 13/γ = 12 metres to the observer it flies past — 12 &lt; 13. Space shortens as speed climbs. — <a href="/theorem/length_contraction">proof</a>.</li><li>Mass is energy: E = mc², so (with c² = 9 in these units) masses [1,2,3] carry rest energies [9,18,27] — linear in mass. Even at rest, matter holds mc² of energy. — <a href="/theorem/rest_energy_mc2">proof</a>.</li><li>Causality forbids faster-than-light links: a spacelike separation (ct = 3, x = 5) has s² = 9 − 25 = −16 &lt; 0 — outside the light cone, so no signal can connect the events without exceeding c. What is spacelike cannot be a cause. — <a href="/theorem/causality_forbids_ftl">proof</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="provenance" tabindex="-1">Provenance <a class="header-anchor" href="#provenance" aria-label="Permalink to “Provenance”">​</a></h2><p>These 8 proofs fold, order-invariant, to the receipt <code>873b63d2-3fa3-8570-b5c0-d11523b4bb3e</code> — recompute it from the same ledger and it returns. The note itself content-addresses to a uuid, so any edit is visible. Writing descends from reading: this note holds only what the proofs it links already sealed, and it was audited by uuidna&#39;s own honesty gate before it was published — a sentence that overreached a proof would have been refused, not shipped.</p><p>Source · <a href="https://github.com/uuidna/uuidna/blob/main/lean/Relativity.lean" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">lean/Relativity.lean</a> · <a href="/theorems">all theorems</a></p><hr><p><strong>Audited before published</strong> · this note passed uuidna&#39;s honesty gate at build time — every claim above links the proof that seals it. Content-address <code>b8265847</code> · proofs fold to receipt <code>873b63d2</code> (the handles; the full uuids are in this page&#39;s meta, recomputable) · 8 sealed theorems.</p><p><a href="/publications">All publications</a> · <a href="/theorems">All theorems</a> · <a href="/trials">How auditing works</a></p>`,11)]])}var s=e(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};